# What a level 1 mortal is told they cannot do.
#
# Half of this is the command table's own minimum levels, which are part of
# *matching* rather than a check afterwards (5i-a): an immortal command typed
# by a mortal is not refused, it is not found, and the answer is "Huh?!?".
# The other half is minimum_position, cmd_info[]'s second column (5j).
#
# The god is created and dismissed first only because the first character on
# an empty roster would otherwise be one.
Parityone
y
swordfish
swordfish
m
w

1
quit
!reconnect
Paritythree
y
swordfish
swordfish
m
t

1
score
practice
skills
spells
# Immortal commands, which a mortal cannot even match.
goto 3001
load obj 3021
shutdown
wizlock
set Paritythree level 34
users
# Positions: cmd_info[]'s minimum_position, which nothing had been reading
# until 5j.
sleep
north
look
stand
sit
north
stand
# And a word that is not a command at all.
frobnicate
quit
